facts:
The **angle between two non-zero vectors** is measured with the vectors drawn tail to tail, and $0^{\circ}\le\theta\le180^{\circ}$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{angles, quotes, arrows.meta}
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\coordinate (A) at (4,0);
\coordinate (B) at (2.1,3.1);
\draw[-{Stealth}] (O) -- (A) node[midway, below] {$\underset{\sim}{a}$};
\draw[-{Stealth}] (O) -- (B) node[midway, above left] {$\underset{\sim}{b}$};
\pic[draw, "$\theta$", angle radius=0.7cm, angle eccentricity=2] {angle = A--O--B};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

workedExamples.question_text:
Find the exact value of $\underset{\sim}{a}\cdot\underset{\sim}{b}$ for the vectors shown.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black},draw=black]
\usetikzlibrary{arrows.meta}
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\coordinate (A) at (4,0);
\coordinate (B) at (135:3);
\draw[-{Stealth},thick] (O)--(A);
\draw[-{Stealth},thick] (O)--(B);
\path (2,0) node[below] {$|\underset{\sim}{a}|=9$};
\path (-1.1,2.8) node[anchor=west] {$|\underset{\sim}{b}|=2\sqrt{2}$};
\draw (0.7,0) arc[start angle=0,end angle=135,radius=0.7];
\path (67.5:1.05) node {$135^{\circ}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Vectors $\underset{\sim}{p}$ and $\underset{\sim}{q}$ have magnitudes $4$ and $9$. Find their dot product when they point:
(a) in the same direction;
(b) in opposite directions.

